# Job Hunter Agent — Environment Variables
# Copy this file to .env and fill in values as needed.
# NEVER commit the real .env file to version control.
# .env is listed in .gitignore — it will not be tracked.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GMAIL OAUTH (REQUIRED for Gmail outreach feature)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These are NOT stored here. Instead:
#   1. Download credentials.json from Google Cloud Console (see below).
#   2. Place it in the project root: d:\job_hunter_agent\credentials.json
#   3. Run the app and click "Connect Gmail" — a browser window will open
#      Google's consent screen. Sign in and approve. token.json is saved.
#
# Setup steps:
#   1. Go to https://console.cloud.google.com/
#   2. Create a project (e.g. "Job Hunter Agent")
#   3. APIs & Services → Library → search "Gmail API" → Enable
#   4. APIs & Services → Credentials → Create Credentials → OAuth client ID
#      Application type: Desktop application
#      Name: Job Hunter Agent
#   5. Download the JSON and save as: d:\job_hunter_agent\credentials.json
#   6. APIs & Services → OAuth consent screen:
#      - Add your Gmail address as a Test User
#      - Add scope: https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.send
#
# Files created automatically (NEVER commit these):
#   credentials.json  ← you download this once from Google Cloud Console
#   token.json        ← created automatically after OAuth consent
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL: Greenhouse API key (only for private boards with auth)
# Public boards do NOT require a key. Most job boards work without this.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GREENHOUSE_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL: Lever API key (only for private partner API access)
# Public v0 postings endpoint does NOT require a key.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LEVER_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FUTURE: LLM provider for AI-assisted resume tailoring
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FUTURE: Slack notifications
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HOSTED DEPLOYMENT
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local development can leave these unset. On a hosted service:
# APP_ENV=production
# APP_PASSWORD=<set a long, unique password in the host's secret settings>
# JOB_HUNTER_DATA_DIR=/var/data
# JOB_HUNTER_DB_PATH=/var/data/jobs.db
# Never paste deployment secrets into chat or commit them to this file.
